t3oxide third-party attribution

The active SLT runtime is a maintained vendored SuperLightTUI 0.26.0 (MIT),
base d4537d74f4b42188e06cb224fbfe7684397897fb with ordered-activation-v1.
vendor/superlighttui/UPSTREAM.md identifies packaging and modified files;
vendor/superlighttui/LICENSE retains the complete upstream MIT notice.

The Rust terminal client directly uses Ratatui 0.30.2 (MIT), ratatui-textarea
0.9.3 (MIT), tui-markdown 0.3.13 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), and nucleo-matcher 0.3.1
(MPL-2.0), together with the crates recorded in Cargo.lock.

LICENSES/rust-third-party.txt contains the original license and notice texts
for the complete locked Rust dependency graph. docs/dependencies.json records
exact versions, source archive URLs, checksums and upstream commit identities
where available. Include NOTICE and LICENSES/ with binary distributions.

nucleo-matcher is used as an unmodified library. Its MPL-2.0-covered source is
available at https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/nucleo-matcher/0.3.1/download,
with the archive checksum in Cargo.lock and docs/dependencies.json. No upstream
MPL-covered file is copied into or modified within the application source.

Herdr, Herdr T3 Focus, Herdr T3 layout and TUIOS informed interaction choices;
their application code is not bundled. No FrankenTUI code or restricted course
material is incorporated. docs/rust-source-reuse.md records exact inspected
sources, licenses and adoption decisions.

The notices below cover retained Node adapter contract and codec adaptations.
They do not grant a top-level license to t3oxide's original application code.

adapter/core.mjs, adapter/t3.mjs, adapter/models.mjs, adapter/navigation.mjs
and adapter/native.mjs
adapt narrow command, response, catalog, lineage and event
structures from pingdotgg/t3code at 0e7346ccd9427c06161e222319e718e6bd70887f.
adapter/wire.mjs implements the narrow Effect RPC envelopes documented in that
repository's .repos/effect-smol RpcMessage.ts. These are adapted client-side
contracts, not a bundled copy of the full T3 runtime. See docs/architecture.md
and docs/model-navigation.md.

Native workflow extension 1 independently implements bounded project/default,
launch, inbox lifecycle and review presentation over those verified native
contracts. Its JSONC/default-file behavior follows the pinned public contract;
it bundles no Effect schema runtime or native execution service. See
docs/native-workflows.md for exact source references and compatibility limits.

adapter/core.mjs also adapts native lossless bounded snapshot restoration from
pingdotgg/t3code a773dc38ac75177b6cd133d27df00ca0a83f9480:
packages/contracts/src/orchestrationV2IdTable.ts and
packages/shared/src/orchestrationV2BoundedSnapshot.ts and
orchestrationV2DedupedBodies.ts. This is a narrow MIT-licensed codec adaptation;
no native runtime is bundled.

